####################################################################################
# Finding #3 — single-blockhash budget exhaustion
#   (poc_03_blockhash_budget.py)
####################################################################################
MultiHopper finding #3 — single-blockhash budget vs prescribed broadcast waits
One /prepare -> one blockhash (lifetime ~60s) must cover ALL four groups.

### Documented worst case — keeper confirm within its own 60s poll
    per-confirm latency: keeper=55s route=10s orch=10s session=10s | n_route=2 n_session=1
    group                broadcast @ t   blockhash status
    keeperFundingTx              0.0s   valid
    routeInitTxs[0]             55.0s   valid
    routeInitTxs[1]             65.0s   EXPIRED — tx rejected (BlockhashNotFound)
    orchestratorInitTx          78.0s   EXPIRED — tx rejected (BlockhashNotFound)
    sessionInitTxs[0]           91.0s   EXPIRED — tx rejected (BlockhashNotFound)
    total elapsed before final group broadcast: 91.0s (blockhash lifetime 60s)
    => 'routeInitTxs[1]' onward broadcast against an EXPIRED blockhash -> forced into the resume path

### Realistic devnet latencies
    per-confirm latency: keeper=20s route=15s orch=15s session=15s | n_route=3 n_session=2
    group                broadcast @ t   blockhash status
    keeperFundingTx              0.0s   valid
    routeInitTxs[0]             20.0s   valid
    routeInitTxs[1]             35.0s   valid
    routeInitTxs[2]             50.0s   valid
    orchestratorInitTx          68.0s   EXPIRED — tx rejected (BlockhashNotFound)
    sessionInitTxs[0]           86.0s   EXPIRED — tx rejected (BlockhashNotFound)
    sessionInitTxs[1]          101.0s   EXPIRED — tx rejected (BlockhashNotFound)
    total elapsed before final group broadcast: 101.0s (blockhash lifetime 60s)
    => 'orchestratorInitTx' onward broadcast against an EXPIRED blockhash -> forced into the resume path

### Optimistic — fast confirmations everywhere
    per-confirm latency: keeper=8s route=8s orch=8s session=8s | n_route=3 n_session=2
    group                broadcast @ t   blockhash status
    keeperFundingTx              0.0s   valid
    routeInitTxs[0]              8.0s   valid
    routeInitTxs[1]             16.0s   valid
    routeInitTxs[2]             24.0s   valid
    orchestratorInitTx          35.0s   valid
    sessionInitTxs[0]           46.0s   valid
    sessionInitTxs[1]           54.0s   valid
    total elapsed before final group broadcast: 54.0s (blockhash lifetime 60s)
    => fits within one blockhash

==============================================================================
CONCLUSION
  A single shared blockhash cannot reliably cover the prescribed
  'confirm each group before the next + 3s delays' procedure. Under the
  documented keeper poll alone (up to 60s) the route group can already be
  expired; under realistic devnet latency the happy path is regularly
  blown, making the resume path the norm rather than the exception.
==============================================================================

