# Finding #4 — preparedTxs.resume.* is undocumented
#   (poc_04_resume_undocumented.py)
####################################################################################
MultiHopper finding #4 — `resume` is read by the reference code but undocumented

preparedTxs fields READ by the documented reference loop:
    preparedTxs.resume.nothingToDo
    preparedTxs.resume.routeAlreadyDeployed

preparedTxs fields DEFINED by the documentation:
    preparedTxs.keeperFundingTx
    preparedTxs.lastValidBlockHeight
    preparedTxs.orchestratorInitTx
    preparedTxs.recentBlockhash
    preparedTxs.routeInitTxs
    preparedTxs.sessionInitTxs

UNDOCUMENTED fields the reference code depends on:
    preparedTxs.resume.nothingToDo    <-- not in any documented schema
    preparedTxs.resume.routeAlreadyDeployed    <-- not in any documented schema

Impact: loop termination in the reference 'Full autonomous loop' branches on
`preparedTxs.resume?.nothingToDo` and `?.routeAlreadyDeployed`. With `resume`
undocumented, an agent generating its own client cannot know these exist and
its termination logic diverges from the reference (premature exit, or looping
until the attempt cap throws despite the transfer having progressed).

